From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:35:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Payroll: fill the absent deduction from guard attendance

Absent deduction = days marked Absent in the salary month x daily rate.
The daily rate rule is a Finance setting (basic or basic + allowances,
divided by days in the month, 30 or 26; default basic / days in month).

- Filled automatically when a month's salaries are added (can be turned off).
- Payroll > Absent deductions: preview against what each salary holds now and
  apply after late attendance changes; totals move by the difference.
- Only employees with attendance that month; paid salaries never change;
  sign-ins awaiting review are warned about, not counted.
- Every change logged in absent_deduction_changes.
- Salary upload: totals now use the absent amount actually saved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CtfNpegKha8zDfMKmDrDiS
